  "doc": "Rubble patterns of destroyed buildings (tactical battle). `floorHeight` = m per floor when the building height is unknown. `materials` (light|brick|concrete|reinforced, from the building's material class): heap height = clamp(min(original height, heightCap) * heightFrac * (area/150)^areaGain, minHeight, maxHeight) (house 2 floors -> 2-3 m, 8 floors -> 5-8 m); `fill` = fraction of the footprint the heap covers; `spill` = [min,max] m the heap overflows into the street (grows with the footprint); `scatter` = share of loose pieces thrown out onto the spill zone; `density` = loose pieces per 100 m2 (between minPieces and maxPieces; the cap bounds the triangle count: 12 per piece, walls included); `palette` = piece tints [r,g,b] (the original material, so the player recognises what stood there); `textures` = ids of the atlas in buildings.json used by the pieces; `pieces` = weighted list of block | slab | beam with `size` (longest side, m) and `thickness` (m, slab/beam); `walls` = fragments of wall left standing at the heap edge with the facade texture (windows): count = clamp(perimeter*perMetre, min, max), width/height/thickness ranges (m), lean (rad), textures; `rebar` = share of beams that stick out of the heap; `mound` = the heap body (tint + texture + roughness 0..1); `decal` = darkened rubble/dust stain on the ground (color + margin [min,max] m beyond the heap foot). `collapse` per cause (by): duration (s of battle time), tilt (deg), shrinkTo (height fraction left of the standing building at the end), shake (m of tremor), dust (puffs per second), blocks (falling blocks per second), style down = vertical sink | breach = the wall is knocked through away from the breaching vehicle. `dust` (real seconds, render only): the cloud (cloudPuffs big puffs at the fall, cloudLife [min,max] s, cloudGrow growth factor, cloudAlpha peak opacity) then thin residual smoke from the heap (smokeEvery s between puffs, smokeLife [min,max] s per puff, smokeAlpha opacity, smokeTime [min,max] s the heap keeps smoking, maxSmoking = heaps smoking at once (the most recent), maxPuffs = cap of live puffs).",
